<title>INDIA: Indian oil pipeline burst sparks massive fire.</title>
<headline>Indian oil pipeline burst sparks massive fire.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>An oil pipeline exploded early on Thursday morning in India's northeastern state of Assam, triggering a massive fire, the United News of India (UNI) newsagency reported.</p>
<p>The pipeline, carrying crude oil and owned by the state-run Oil India Ltd (OIL), exploded at Bijulighat near Nalbari, about 55 kms from the state capital of Guwahati, UNI said. There was no immediate confirmation of the explosion or any reports of casualties.</p>
</text>
